yjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T16:20:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T16:20:18Z","body":"@dt10812 I don't believe you. Not only did you use the exact PR template style used by AI (and no human contributors), you also included \"Verified that all affected changes are limited to scene/3d/physics/physical_bone_3d.cpp.\" in your testing steps. That doesn't make any sense, if you wrote the code, why do you need to go and verify which files it touched? Further you claimed that Github actions had completed successfully before they had even run! \r\n\r\nWe don't ban people for using AI to generate their PR comments. But we can't accept a PR that violates our policy. My suggestion is to try again with another PR, but avoid using AI this time. Even if you wrote the code by hand and then used an AI to generate the PR description, we can't be certain so we need to reject the entire PR. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4951891354/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4953344863","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121257#issuecomment-4953344863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121257","id":4953344863,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJz4LXw","user":{"login":"dt10812","id":176304559,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoIxrw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176304559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812","html_url":"https://github.com/dt10812","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T00:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T00:12:36Z","body":"> @dt10812 I don't believe you. Not only did you use the exact PR template style used by AI (and no human contributors), you also included \"Verified that all affected changes are limited to scene/3d/physics/physical_bone_3d.cpp.\" in your testing steps. That doesn't make any sense, if you wrote the code, why do you need to go and verify which files it touched? Further you claimed that Github actions had completed successfully before they had even run!\r\n> \r\n> We don't ban people for using AI to generate their PR comments. But we can't accept a PR that violates our policy. My suggestion is to try again with another PR, but avoid using AI this time. Even if you wrote the code by hand and then used an AI to generate the PR description, we can't be certain so we need to reject the entire PR.\r\n\r\nLet me explain my description : The statement \"Verified that all affected changes are limited to the file\" meant that I made sure that the changes don't affect other files. Also I set up Github Actions on my fork and you could see it. But I did admitted that the PR template is generated using AI but with a round of editions by me.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4953344863/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4953355853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121257#issuecomment-4953355853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121257","id":4953355853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJz42TQ","user":{"login":"dt10812","id":176304559,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoIxrw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176304559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812","html_url":"https://github.com/dt10812","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dt10812/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T00:14:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T00:14:49Z","body":"> > @dt10812 I don't believe you. Not only did you use the exact PR template style used by AI (and no human contributors), you also included \"Verified that all affected changes are limited to scene/3d/physics/physical_bone_3d.cpp.\" in your testing steps. That doesn't make any sense, if you wrote the code, why do you need to go and verify which files it touched? Further you claimed that Github actions had completed successfully before they had even run!\r\n> > We don't ban people for using AI to generate their PR comments. But we can't accept a PR that violates our policy. My suggestion is to try again with another PR, but avoid using AI this time. Even if you wrote the code by hand and then used an AI to generate the PR description, we can't be certain so we need to reject the entire PR.\r\n> \r\n> Let me explain my description : The statement \"Verified that all affected changes are limited to the file\" meant that I made sure that the changes don't affect other files. Also I set up Github Actions on my fork and you could see it. But I admit that the PR template is generated using AI but with a round of editions by me.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4953355853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]